%% ======================================================================================
%% CONCIERGE (K1) — UNIFIED END-TO-END ARCHITECTURE
%% ======================================================================================
%% Merged from:
%%   POC: poc/k1_poc/concierge_poc_architecture.mmd (908 lines, battle-tested design)
%%   K1:  k1/concierge/concierge.mmd (1112 lines, hexagonal + services + lifecycle)
%% Created: 2026-04-01
%% Purpose: Single source of truth for ALL Concierge architecture
%%
%% CORE DESIGN PRINCIPLES:
%%   1. The Concierge IS Two Minds:
%%        FRONT LLM (Voice): Warm, empathetic, family-aware. TALKS to user.
%%        BACK LLM (Worker): Precise, tool-focused, no personality. EXECUTES tasks.
%%      Neither knows the other exists. Session State is shared memory.
%%      K1 Event Bus is the communication channel. Events are triggers.
%%
%%   2. Hexagonal Architecture (8 Ports):
%%        All external dependencies accessed through ports.
%%        Internal services call ports, never external systems directly (INV-16).
%%        Each port has a production adapter (real infra) and a test adapter (in-memory).
%%        Circuit breakers live inside production adapters.
%%
%%   3. Single Writer Invariant (ADR-0017):
%%        Concierge is the ONLY writer to SessionState.
%%        Front writes cognitive sections. FSM writes task/system sections.
%%        Back NEVER writes SS directly — emits deltas → bus → FSM applies.
%%        Orchestrator/Planner/Agents NEVER write SS.
%%
%% ACTOR MODEL:
%%   Front LLM: Signal(1) + Cognitive(6) + Read(2) + Control(1) = 10 tools
%%   Back LLM:  Read(2) + Action(3+1) + Control(1) = 7 tools
%%   Both use shared react_loop() function.
%%   Front terminates: text response with NO tool calls.
%%   Back terminates: submit_result() tool call ONLY.
%%
%% FSM STATES (11 coded, 1 proposed):
%%   Core: LISTENING → DISPATCHING → COMPANIONING → PROGRESSING → DELIVERING
%%   Interrupt: CLARIFYING_USER, CLARIFYING_WORKER, CANCELLING, INTERRUPT_HANDLING
%%   Special: PROACTIVE_WAKE, WEAVING
%%   Proposed: BACKGROUND_WORKING (needs ADR-0097)
%%
%% PROMPT MODES (10):
%%   STANDARD, CLARIFY_ASK, CLARIFY_RESOLVE, HITL_RELAY, HITL_RESOLVE,
%%   PRESENT, WEAVE, CANCEL, INTERRUPT, ERROR
%%
%% SESSION STATE: HOT (52KB, 10 sections) + WARM (48KB, 4 sections)
%%
%% COMPLEXITY TIERS:
%%   LOW:    Front → dispatch → Back → invoke_capability() directly (<2s)
%%   MEDIUM: Front → dispatch → OrchestratorStub (1-2 Fabric calls, 2-10s)
%%   HIGH:   Front → TaskEnvelope → Orchestrator → Planner 4-stage (10-45s)
%%
%% OPP PRIMITIVES (8):
%%   OPP-1 Paced Delivery, OPP-2 Recency Bias Decay, OPP-3 Affect Hard Caps,
%%   OPP-4 Trust Accumulator, OPP-5 Proactive Scheduler, OPP-6 Episodic Compression,
%%   OPP-7 Dynamic Identity, OPP-8 Natural Flow Delivery
%%
%% CAUSAL ORDERING:
%%   TimingChain enforces parent_id chains for STRICT topics.
%%
%% HITL PROTOCOL:
%%   Three variants: Clarification (60s), Approval (120s), Selection (90s).
%%   Max 2 suspensions per task. ReAct history preserved on suspend.
%%
%% EXPERIENCE LAYER (6 components, 3 real + 3 stubs):
%%   EmotionalProcessor (25th turn), AffectiveMirror (after EP),
%%   NarrativeWeaver (20th turn, STUB), AnticipatoryResponder (30th turn, STUB),
%%   ProactiveScheduler (OPP-5, STUB), RhythmController (every output)
%%
%% INVARIANTS: 21 non-negotiable rules across 6 categories
%% CIRCUIT BREAKERS: 7 (CB_SSE, CB_MODEL, CB_SESSIONSTATE, CB_ORCHESTRATOR,
%%   CB_PLANNER, CB_FABRIC, CB_MCP)
%% PERFORMANCE: System overhead ~32ms/turn (excluding LLM)
%% LIFECYCLE: 6 phases (init, turn_start, turn_end, turn_end_abbreviated,
%%   shutdown, crash_recovery)
%% INTERNAL SERVICES: 9 codeable components (~585 tests)
%% STREAMING: 8 components (~150 tests)
%% ======================================================================================

